# Statement PDFs are byte-pinned evidence. The forensic audits record a SHA-256
# per source document (docs/balance-metrics-audit-results.csv) and the corpus gate
# re-verifies every one of them, so checkout must reproduce the exact bytes on
# every platform.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default) rewrites any PDF that
# git's heuristic reads as text — a PDF whose first 8000 bytes contain no NUL,
# e.g. one whose image streams are ASCII85-encoded. That silently changed two
# corpus documents' bytes and made the pinned hashes unreproducible.
*.pdf binary

# Other binary evidence and export formats.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.xlsx binary
*.zip binary
